{"id": 10001696, "reference": "A12/01127/20", "publication_date": "2020-08-07T12:48:18.257Z", "modification_date": "2020-08-07T12:48:18.258Z", "country": "Germany", "product_category": "CHEMICAL_PRODUCTS", "product_name": "Tattoo ink", "product_name_specific": "Shamrock", "risk_description": "The product contains an excessive amount of cadmium (measured value: 0.65 ppm). Cadmium is harmful to human health because it accumulates in the body, can damage the kidneys and bones and it may cause cancer. \n\nAdditionally, it contains benzisothiazolinone (measured value: 0,007 %), which is not allowed in cosmetic products,  and, according to the list of ingredients, the colourant pigment yellow 14 (CI 21095), which releases the aromatic amine 3,3'-dichlorobenzidine. This aromatic amine is skin sensitiser and may also cause cancer. \nBenzisothiazolinone is a skin sensitiser and triggers allergic reactions or contact dermatitis.", "legal_provision": "The Council of Europe Resolution ResAP (2008)1 on requirements and criteria for the safety of tattoos and permanent make-up, recommends that the levels of cadmium do not exceed 0,2 ppm, that aromatic amines with carcinogenic mutagenic, reprotoxic or sensitising properties should neither be present nor released from azo-colourants, and that substances forbidden in the Cosmetic Products Regulation are not used.", "country_of_origin": "United States", "sold_online": "UNKNOWN", "notification_type": "ARTICLE_12", "brands": ["FUSION INK"], "model_types": ["FI-069"], "risk_types": ["CHEMICAL"], "measures": ["PRODUCT_WITHDRAWAL_FROM_MARKET"], "embedding_model": "siglip2-b16-256", "embedding_dim": 768, "photos": [{"photo_id": 10014147, "main": true, "embedding": ""}, {"photo_id": 10014148, "main": false, "embedding": ""}]}